title: BADBOX 3.0 Module Repository and Ad-Config Domain Lookup
id: c1a58d34-90f7-4b6e-a2c8-7e430d1fb596
status: experimental
description: Detects DNS resolution of the BADBOX 3.0 module-repository and ad-configuration hosts (drgdj.top self-hosted GitHub proxy and shzhtxcz.com) used by the backdoor on uncertified AOSP TV boxes to pull versioned ad-fraud modules.
references:
  - https://www.humansecurity.com/learn/blog/satori-threat-intelligence-disruption-badbox-3-0-hides-the-largest-ad-fraud-operation-ever-disclosed-inside-infected-tv-boxes/
  - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/badbox-30-botnet-returns-with-record-breaking-40-billion-daily-ad-requests/
  - https://www.securityweek.com/badbox-3-0-ad-fraud-operation-generating-40-billion-daily-bid-requests-disrupted/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/23
tags:
  - attack.t1071
  - attack.t1105
  - attack.t1496
logsource:
  category: dns_query
detection:
  selection:
    QueryName|endswith:
      - 'drgdj.top'
      - 'shzhtxcz.com'
  condition: selection
falsepositives:
  - Unlikely - the domains are attacker-registered for the BADBOX 3.0 module and ad-config service
level: high
